{"strongs": "H5060", "word": "נָגַע", "translit": "na.ga", "root": "נגע", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "touch, reach, strike", "definition": "נָגַע :150 verb touch, reach, strike (Late Hebrew id. ; Arabic is agree with one (of food), produce effect ; Aramaic נְגַע Ithpa`al be struck (that is, with leprosy), compare Pi`el below); — Qal Perfect ׳ נ Gen 32:33 +; נָָֽגְעָה Judg 20:41 +; 1 plural suffix נְנַעֲנוּךָ Gen 26:29 Imperfect יִגַּע Lev 5:3 +; וַיִּגַּע Gen 32:26 +, etc.; Imperative גַּע Ps 144:5 + 2 t.; Infinitive construct נְגֹעַ , לִנְגּוֺעַ Gen 20:6 + 3 t.; גַּ֫עַת 2Sam 14:10 ; Ezek 17:10 suffix נָגְעֵךְ Ruth 2:9 etc.; Participle active נֹגֵעַ 1Kgs 19:5 +; נֹגְעִים Jer 12:14 feminine נֹגַ֫עַת Num 19:22 + 2 t.; plural נֹגְעֹת 1Kgs 6:27 passive נָגוּעַ Ps 73:14 ; Isa 53:4 — 1. a. touch , usually followed by בְּ Gen 3:3 ( J ), Gen 32:25 ; Gen 32:33 ; Exod 19:12 (twice in verse); Exod 19:13 (all E ), Exod 29:37 ; Exod 30:20 ( P ), Lev 5:2 ; Lev 5:3 + 25 t. Leviticus; Num 16:26 + 7 t. Numbers ( P ) + Num 19:22 (no בְּ or object), Deut 14:8 ; Judg 6:21 ; 2Sam 23:7 ; 1Kgs 6:27 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 19:5 ; 1Kgs 19:7 ; 2Kgs 13:21 ; Esth 5:2 ; Dan 8:5 ; Dan 8:18 ; Lam 4:14 followed by אֶלֿ Hag 2:12 ; Num 4:15 ; 1Kgs 6:27 ; Dan 9:21 , compare Hos 4:2 compare עַלפֶּֿה Isa 6:7 עַלשָֿׂפָה Dan 10:16 compare accusative Isa 52:11 absolute (no object expressed) Job 6:7 ; Lam 4:15 . \\ \\ b. of ׳ י touching earth, mountains, etc., followed by בְּ Amos 9:5 ; Ps 104:32 ; Ps 144:5 figurative of ׳ י touching the heart, followed by בְּ 1Sam 10:26 . 2. nearly = strike , passive stricken , Ps 73:14 ; Isa 53:4 || מֻכֶּה ), of wind Job 1:19 ; Ezek 17:10 of divine chastisement 1Sam 6:9 ; Job 1:11 ; Job 19:21 followed by אֶל Job 2:5 . 3. touch = harm, followed by. בְּ , Gen 26:11 ( J ), Josh 9:19 ; 2Sam 14:10 ; 1Chr 16:22 || הָרֵעַ ) = Ps 105:15 ; Jer 12:14 ; Zech 2:12 (twice in verse); followed by. אֶלֿ Gen 20:6 ( touch a woman), so Prov 6:29 (followed by בְּ ); followed by. accusative Gen 26:29 ( J , suffix), so Ruth 2:9 see also Job 5:19 (subject רַע , followed by בְּ ), Judg 20:34 ; Judg 20:41 (both subject רָעָה , followed by עַלֿ ). 4. reach, extend to , 2Sam 5:8 , followed by בְּ (but corrupt see Dr HPS ); in metaphor, followed by עַד , of vine Isa 16:8 ; Jer 48:32 of sword Jer 4:10 , compare v Jer 4:18 of chastisement Mic 1:9 , compare Job 4:5 (|| בּוֺא אֶלֿ ); also (followed by אֶל ) Jer 51:9 = come , followed by אֶלֿ Jonah 3:6 arrive (of time), absolute Ezra 3:1 ; Neh 7:73 . Niph`al Imperfect וַיִּנָָּֽנְעוּ Josh 8:15 be stricken, defeated (in battle), i.e. feign to be so, but read probably וַיִּנָָּֽגְפוּ , see נגף Niph`al Pi`el Perfect suffix נִגְּעוֺ 2Chr 26:20 strike (with leprosy, 2 accusative), subject ׳ י ; so Imperfect וַיְנַגַּע 2Kgs 15:5 ; Gen 12:17 (subject ׳ י ; accusative of person + accusative of cognate meaning). Pu`al Imperfect יְנֻגָּע֑וּ be sticken by diseases (?; compare Pi`el and נֶגַע 2. 3. especially 2Sam 7:14 ) Ps 73:5 . Hiph`il Perfect הִגִּיעַ Isa 25:12 + 6 t.; 2 feminine singular הִגַּ֫עַתְּ Esth 4:14 1 singular suffix וְהִגַּעְתִּ֫יהוּ Ezek 13:14 , etc.; Imperfect יַגִּיעַ Isa 8:8 + 3 t.; וַיַּגַּע Isa 6:7 ; Jer 1:9 , etc.; Infinitive construct הַגִּיעַ Esth 2:12 ; Esth 2:15 Participle מַגִּיעַ Gen 28:12 +; feminine מַגַּ֫עַת 2Chr 3:11 — cause to touch; reach, approach, arrive: 1. cause to touch, apply , Exod 12:22 ) ( J E ; מִדָּם , אֶלֿ ); cause to touch (compare עַד עָפָר , לָאָרֶץ ), i.e. bring to ground, Isa 25:5 ; Isa 25:12 , compare Lam 2:2 ; Ezek 13:14 (followed by אֶלֿ ), Exod 4:25 ( J ; followed by לְרַגְלָיו ); followed by עַלפֶּֿה Isa 6:7 ; Jer 1:9 followed by בְּ Isa 5:8 . 2. intransitive reach, extend , Gen 28:12 (followed by ָ ה locative); followed by אֶלֿ Zech 14:5 , followed by עַד Isa 8:8 compare ׳ תַּגּ יָדוֺ דֵּי שֶׂה Lev 5:7 if his hand do not reach enough for a lamb (i.e. he be not able to furnish a lamb); followed by לְ Job 20:6 (hyperbole) 2Chr 3:11 (twice in verse); 2Chr 3:12 followed by עַד לְ 2Chr 28:9 attain , followed by לְ Esth 4:14 , arrive, come , followed by accusative of location Isa 30:4 ; Esth 4:3 ; Esth 8:17 , followed by לְ (of time) Dan 12:12 , followed by אֶלֿ 1Sam 14:9 , followed by עַדֿ Ps 107:18 , absolute Esth 6:14 followed by אֵצֶל Dan 8:7 . 3. approach , of time, absolute Eccl 12:1 ; Song 2:12 ; Ezek 7:12 (|| בּוֺא ); see also Esth 9:1 (followed by Infinitive), compare Esth 2:12 ; Esth 2:15 ; Ps 88:4 (followed by לְ ). 4. of fate or lot, = befal , followed by אֶלֿ Esth 9:26 ; Eccl 8:14 (twice in verse); Ps 32:6 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4976')\">BDB4976</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5060')\">H5060</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4975')\">BDB4975</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4977')\">BDB4977</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>נָגַע</bdbheb> :150 <b>verb</b> <highlightword>touch, reach, strike</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder3173/> is <highlight>agree</highlight> with one (of food), <highlight>produce effect</highlight>; Aramaic <bdbarc>נְגַע</bdbarc> Ithpa`al <highlight>be struck</highlight> (that is, with leprosy), compare Pi`el below); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>נ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 32:33\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(1,32,33)\">Gen 32:33</ref> +; <bdbheb>נָָֽגְעָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 20:41\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"41\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"41\" onclick=\"bcv(7,20,41)\">Judg 20:41</ref> +; 1 plural suffix <bdbheb>נְנַעֲנוּךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 26:29\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,29)\">Gen 26:29</ref> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>יִגַּע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 5:3\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(3,5,3)\">Lev 5:3</ref> +; <bdbheb>וַיִּגַּע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 32:26\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(1,32,26)\">Gen 32:26</ref> +, etc.; <highlight>Imperative</highlight> <bdbheb>גַּע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 144:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"144\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"144\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,144,5)\">Ps 144:5</ref> + 2 t.; <highlight>Infinitive construct</highlight> <bdbheb>נְגֹעַ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>לִנְגּוֺעַ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 20:6\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(1,20,6)\">Gen 20:6</ref> + 3 t.; <bdbheb>גַּ֫עַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 14:10\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(10,14,10)\">2Sam 14:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 17:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,17,10)\">Ezek 17:10</ref> suffix <bdbheb>נָגְעֵךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ruth 2:9\" b=\"8\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(8,2,9)\">Ruth 2:9</ref> etc.; <highlight>Participle active</highlight> <bdbheb>נֹגֵעַ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 19:5\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(11,19,5)\">1Kgs 19:5</ref> +; <bdbheb>נֹגְעִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 12:14\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(24,12,14)\">Jer 12:14</ref> feminine <bdbheb>נֹגַ֫עַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 19:22\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(4,19,22)\">Num 19:22</ref> + 2 t.; plural <bdbheb>נֹגְעֹת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 6:27\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(11,6,27)\">1Kgs 6:27</ref> <highlight>passive</highlight> <bdbheb>נָגוּעַ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 73:14\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"73\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"73\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(19,73,14)\">Ps 73:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 53:4\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"53\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"53\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(23,53,4)\">Isa 53:4</ref> — </div><div class=\"point\"><b>1. a.</b> <highlight>touch</highligh